The Sliding Window Logic
To generate edges, your engine must iterate through the tokenized text. If "Character A" and "Character B" both appear within a window of $N$ words (typically 50–100), an edge is created[cite: 1, 2].Edge Weight: Each subsequent appearance in the same window increases the weight by $+1$.  Distance Decay (Advanced): You can implement a formula where the weight $W$ is calculated as $W = 1 / d$, where $d$ is the number of words separating the two entities.4. Next Steps for Portfolio ImpactDocumentation: In your Engine README, include a "Quick Start" that allows a recruiter to run the pipeline on a sample text with one command.  Narrative: In the Data README, write a "Comparative Insight" section. For example, explain why the Mahabharata graph might show higher Clustering Coefficients (tight-knit family units) compared to the more linear genealogical structures in parts of the Hebrew Bible[cite: 1, 2].